<p>Care Core is one system of record for everyone connected to a care organisation: the <strong>staff</strong> who work there, the <strong>people they support</strong>, and the <strong>teams</strong> that connect them.</p>

<h2>The problem it solves</h2>
<p>Most care organisations keep the same facts in several places: an HR system, a rota, a training tracker, a care system, a spreadsheet of registrations. When someone joins, moves team or leaves, somebody has to remember to update every one of them. Things get missed. The classic failures are a leaver who is still in a team, still listed as someone’s key worker, and still able to sign in.</p>
<p>Care Core removes the copying. There is one database and one record of each person. Joining, moving and leaving are single actions that change everything that depends on them at the same moment, and then tell the other systems.</p>

<h2>What is in it</h2>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Can be switched off?</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>People</strong></td><td>One permanent record for every person, search, profile pages, the activity log, tasks, logins and approvals.</td><td>No: it is the core.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Staff</strong></td><td>Joiner, mover and leaver processes, the full staff record (personal details, pay and tax, TUPE, working time, visas, apprenticeships, leave), registrations, supervisions, appraisals, learning, self-service and approvals.</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Teams</strong></td><td>Hierarchies of teams and services, who is in each and for how long, staff-only teams.</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Care</strong></td><td>People we support: support episodes, care needs, contacts and key workers.</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>How it differs from a set of separate apps</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>One person, many roles.</strong> A bank worker who is also a relative of someone you support, or a support worker who becomes a manager, is still one person with one history.</li>
<li><strong>Everything has dates.</strong> Employment, team membership and key worker links are periods with a start and an end. You can always answer “who was in this team in March?”.</li>
<li><strong>Nothing is deleted.</strong> A leaver’s history stays. A rehire is a new employment for the same person, not a duplicate.</li>
<li><strong>Changes are all-or-nothing.</strong> A leaver cannot be half-leaving. The employment, the team places, the key worker links, the login, the checklist, the audit record and the outgoing event are written in one transaction.</li>
<li><strong>Other systems are told, not asked to poll.</strong> Every change creates an event that can be delivered as a signed webhook. Microsoft Entra can also push joiners and leavers in.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who it is for</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Registered managers and team leaders</strong> who need to know who is on their team today and what is due.</li>
<li><strong>HR and administrators</strong> who start, move and end staff and keep the compliance records.</li>
<li><strong>Staff</strong> who keep their own details up to date and see their own job, team and records.</li>
<li><strong>IT</strong> who connect Microsoft Entra, webhooks and other systems.</li>
</ul>

